IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Criminal Code Act Compilation Act 1913 (Western Australia), Appendix B, The Criminal Code -- a narrow slice for two
-- life events: the age of criminal responsibility (s 29); who takes part in an offence (s 7); an honest claim of right
-- (s 22); what can be stolen and what stealing is (ss 370, 371); the penalty for stealing and its special cases (s 378);
-- the summary conviction penalties for stealing (ss 426, 426A) and the summary trial rule (s 5); threats (ss 338, 338A,
-- 338B, with "circumstances of aggravation" in s 221 and "circumstances of racial aggravation" in s 80I); and criminal
-- damage and damaging property (ss 444, 445).
--
-- SEAT: the accused person (Jake at 15, charged with stealing) and, for threats and damage, the victim (Jake at 29, whose
-- door is painted and lock glued over a friend's debt). The accused asks "Can I be held responsible at my age?",
-- "Did I steal it?", "What is the most I can get?". The victim asks "What offence was committed against me?" and "What is
-- the most the offender faces?". Where the Code hands a judgment to the court or the jury (whether behaviour "may
-- reasonably be regarded" as a threat; whether capacity under s 29 "is proved"; whether a taking was fraudulent outside
-- the s 371(2) intents; whether the court sends a charge for trial on indictment under s 5(3)), the answer is conditional
-- on that judgment, which is asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: s 5(1)-(3) (as far as the summary-or-indictment question), s 7 (first paragraph), s 22 (second
-- paragraph), s 29, s 80I, s 221(1), (1A), s 338, s 338A, s 338B(1) and its summary conviction penalty, s 370 (first two
-- paragraphs worked out; the animal paragraphs asked as one fact), s 371(1), (2), (5), (6), s 378 (head and (1), (2),
-- (4a), (5)-(9)), s 426(1)-(5), s 426A, s 444(1A), (1) and its summary conviction penalty, s 445.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (law 196, mrdoc 49336, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49336.txt. The deposit names no compilation number. Its compilation table ends with
-- the Education and Care Services National Law Application Act 2026 Pt 6 Div 7 (in force 1 May 2026); the uncommenced
-- provisions table lists the Prostitution Amendment Act 2008 s 30, the Evidence Act 2025 Pt 12 Div 10 and the Assisted
-- Reproductive Technology and Surrogacy Act 2025 Pt 17 Div 5 (to be proclaimed; not shown, not encoded). No regulations
-- set a number used here: every number ($1 000, $10 000, $50 000, the fines, the terms, the ages 10, 14 and 60) is the
-- Code's own. This is the law as deposited in 2026; the 2021 event is answered on it. s 426 was last amended and s 426A
-- inserted by the Criminal Code Amendment Act 2024 (No. 16 of 2024, in force 1 July 2024), so the summary penalty for an
-- offence in 2021 may have differed; the earlier text is not deposited.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: everything else in a very large Code. In particular: attempts and incitement (s 4, s 552-555A); common
-- purpose (s 8); the other excuses in Chapter V (mistake, s 24; accident, s 23B; duress, s 32; etc.) beyond s 22 and s 29;
-- the offences analogous to stealing and alternative offences (ss 379-424, 429); robbery (s 392); receiving (s 414);
-- motor vehicle stealing by use (s 371A, noted only); stalking (s 338E) and false threats (s 338C); s 444A and s 445A;
-- the rest of Part V and Part VI; sentencing itself (the Sentencing Act 1995; for a young person, the Young Offenders Act
-- 1994, which governs what a court may actually do to Jake at 15 -- see that Act's own encoding); the Criminal Procedure
-- Act 2004 beyond s 5's reference to it; and the Restraining Orders Act 1997 (borrowed by s 221 for "family
-- relationship" and the order, both asked as facts).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The Criminal Code (WA)`

§§ `numbers and helpers`

-- s 29: "under the age of 10 years"; "under the age of 14 years".
`the age of no responsibility` MEANS 10
`the age of presumed capacity` MEANS 14

-- s 378: "imprisonment for 7 years" and the special cases.
`plain stealing years` MEANS 7
`special case years` MEANS 10
`aggravated stealing years` MEANS 14
`reckless motor vehicle stealing years` MEANS 8

-- s 378(5)(b): "its value exceeds $10 000".
`the dwelling value threshold` MEANS 10000

-- s 426(2): "does not exceed $50 000"; s 426(4): "does not exceed $1 000".
`the summary value ceiling` MEANS 50000
`the fine-only value ceiling` MEANS 1000

-- s 426A(2)(b): "at least 2 offences ... within the period of 1 year".
`the previous stealing convictions that end the fine-only penalty` MEANS 2

-- s 444 summary conviction penalty: "the amount of the injury done does not exceed $50 000".
`the damage summary ceiling` MEANS 50000

-- s 221(1)(d): "of or over the age of 60 years" (asked as a fact; kept here as the gloss).

GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `on`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF     DATE_MONTH `on` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `born on`
        OR (DATE_MONTH `on` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `born on` AND DATE_DAY `on` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `born on`)
    THEN DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on` MINUS 1

-- A maximum term: life imprisonment, or a number of years.
DECLARE `Maximum imprisonment` IS ONE OF
    `life imprisonment`
    `years of imprisonment` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER

-- A summary conviction penalty, in the Code's own pairs of imprisonment and fine.
DECLARE `Summary penalty` IS ONE OF
    `a fine only` HAS `the fine` IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment and a fine` HAS `months` IS A NUMBER
                                  `the fine` IS A NUMBER
    `no summary conviction penalty`

§§ `29 -- immature age`

-- s 29: "A person under the age of 10 years is not criminally responsible for any act or omission.
-- A person under the age of 14 years is not criminally responsible for an act or omission, unless it is proved that at the
-- time of doing the act or making the omission he had capacity to know that he ought not to do the act or make the
-- omission." The test is the age at the time of the act. Whether capacity "is proved" is for the court: asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Responsibility at my age` IS ONE OF
    `not criminally responsible, under 10`
    `responsible only if capacity to know is proved, 10 to 13`
    `criminally responsible as anyone is, 14 or over`

@export How does The Criminal Code s 29 treat someone of my age at the time of the act?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date of the act` IS A DATE @desc The date of the act or omission you are accused of
GIVETH A `Responsibility at my age`
DECIDE `How does s 29 treat me at my age` IS
    IF `age in completed years` `my date of birth` `the date of the act` LESS THAN `the age of no responsibility`
    THEN `not criminally responsible, under 10`
    ELSE IF `age in completed years` `my date of birth` `the date of the act` LESS THAN `the age of presumed capacity`
         THEN `responsible only if capacity to know is proved, 10 to 13`
         ELSE `criminally responsible as anyone is, 14 or over`

@export Can I be criminally responsible for what I did at my age (The Criminal Code s 29)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date of the act` IS A DATE @desc The date of the act or omission you are accused of
      `it is proved I knew I ought not to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the prosecution proves that, at the time, you had capacity to know you ought not to do it (needed only if you were 10 to 13)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be criminally responsible at my age` IF
    CONSIDER `How does s 29 treat me at my age` `my date of birth` `the date of the act`
    WHEN `not criminally responsible, under 10` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `responsible only if capacity to know is proved, 10 to 13` THEN `it is proved I knew I ought not to do it`
    WHEN `criminally responsible as anyone is, 14 or over` THEN TRUE

§§ `7 -- principal offenders`

-- s 7: "When an offence is committed, each of the following persons is deemed to have taken part in committing the offence
-- and to be guilty of the offence, and may be charged with actually committing it, that is to say -- (a) Every person who
-- actually does the act ...; (b) Every person who does or omits to do any act for the purpose of enabling or aiding another
-- person to commit the offence; (c) Every person who aids another person in committing the offence; (d) Any person who
-- counsels or procures any other person to commit the offence."
-- Mere presence is in none of the four (an inference from the words; s 8, common purpose, is not encoded).
DECLARE `My part in it` IS ONE OF
    `I did the act myself`
    `I did something to enable or aid another to do it`
    `I aided another in doing it`
    `I counselled or procured another to do it`
    `I was there but did none of those things`

@export Am I taken to have committed the offence with the others (The Criminal Code s 7)?
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in it` @desc What you yourself did
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to have committed it` IF
    CONSIDER `my part`
    WHEN `I was there but did none of those things` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `370, 371, 22 -- what stealing is`

-- s 370: "Every inanimate thing whatever which is the property of any person, and which is movable, is capable of being
-- stolen. Every inanimate thing which is the property of any person, and which is capable of being made movable, is
-- capable of being stolen as soon as it becomes movable". The paragraphs on animals are asked as one fact.
-- s 371(1): "A person who fraudulently takes anything capable of being stolen, or fraudulently converts to his own use or
-- to the use of any other person any property, is said to steal that thing or that property."
-- s 371(2): taking or converting is "deemed to [be done] fraudulently if he does so with any of the following intents"
-- (a)-(f). The deeming is not a complete definition, so a court may still find a taking fraudulent on other grounds:
-- asked as a fact. s 371(3): it "may be fraudulent, although it is effected without secrecy".
-- s 371(5): "When the property converted has been lost by the owner and found by the person who converts it, the
-- conversion is not deemed to be fraudulent if at the time of the conversion the person ... does not know who is the
-- owner, and believes, on reasonable grounds, that the owner cannot be discovered."
-- s 371(6): "The act of stealing is not complete until the person taking or converting the thing actually moves it or
-- otherwise actually deals with it by some physical act."
-- s 22: "a person is not criminally responsible, as for an offence relating to property, for an act done ... with respect
-- to any property in the exercise of an honest claim of right and without intention to defraud."
DECLARE `What I did with the thing` HAS
    `the thing belongs to someone`                                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 370 "the property of any person"
    `the thing is inanimate and movable, or has been made movable`         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 370 first two paragraphs
    `the thing is an animal s 370 makes capable of being stolen`            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 370 animal paragraphs: asked
    `I took it`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(1) "takes"
    `I converted it to my own or someone else's use`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(1) "converts"
    `I meant to keep it from its owner for good`                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(2)(a)
    `I meant to keep someone's special property in it from them for good`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(2)(b): a charge, lien or possessory right
    `I meant to use it as a pledge or security`                            IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(2)(c)
    `I meant to part with it on a condition about its return I might not meet` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(2)(d)
    `I meant to deal with it so it could not be returned in the same condition` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(2)(e)
    `it is money and I meant to use it as I liked, even meaning to repay it` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(2)(f)
    `a court finds it fraudulent on other grounds`                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(1) "fraudulently": a judgment
    `it had been lost and I found it`                                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(5)
    `I knew who the owner was`                                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(5)
    `I believed on reasonable grounds the owner could not be found`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(5)
    `I moved it or physically dealt with it`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 371(6)
    `I acted on an honest claim of right without intent to defraud`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 22

GIVEN `t` IS A `What I did with the thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is capable of being stolen` IF
        `t`'s `the thing belongs to someone`
    AND (   `t`'s `the thing is inanimate and movable, or has been made movable`
         OR `t`'s `the thing is an animal s 370 makes capable of being stolen`)

GIVEN `t` IS A `What I did with the thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I had a s 371(2) intent` IF
       `t`'s `I meant to keep it from its owner for good`
    OR `t`'s `I meant to keep someone's special property in it from them for good`
    OR `t`'s `I meant to use it as a pledge or security`
    OR `t`'s `I meant to part with it on a condition about its return I might not meet`
    OR `t`'s `I meant to deal with it so it could not be returned in the same condition`
    OR `t`'s `it is money and I meant to use it as I liked, even meaning to repay it`

GIVEN `t` IS A `What I did with the thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was fraudulent` IF
    `I had a s 371(2) intent` `t` OR `t`'s `a court finds it fraudulent on other grounds`

-- s 371(5) protects only a conversion of lost property by its finder.
GIVEN `t` IS A `What I did with the thing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the finder's protection applies` IF
        `t`'s `it had been lost and I found it`
    AND (NOT `t`'s `I knew who the owner was`)
    AND `t`'s `I believed on reasonable grounds the owner could not be found`

@export Did I steal it, as The Criminal Code s 371 defines stealing (with s 370)?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did with the thing` @desc The thing, what you did with it, and what you meant to do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I steal it` IF
        (   (    `what I did`'s `I took it`
             AND `the thing is capable of being stolen` `what I did`
             AND `it was fraudulent` `what I did`)
         OR (    `what I did`'s `I converted it to my own or someone else's use`
             AND `it was fraudulent` `what I did`
             AND (NOT `the finder's protection applies` `what I did`)))
    AND `what I did`'s `I moved it or physically dealt with it`

@export Can I be guilty of stealing it, given my age and any honest claim of right (The Criminal Code ss 371, 22, 29)?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did with the thing` @desc The thing, what you did with it, and what you meant to do
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the date of the act` IS A DATE @desc The date you took or converted it
      `it is proved I knew I ought not to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether capacity to know you ought not to do it is proved (needed only if you were 10 to 13)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be guilty of stealing it` IF
        `Did I steal it` `what I did`
    AND (NOT `what I did`'s `I acted on an honest claim of right without intent to defraud`)
    AND `Can I be criminally responsible at my age` `my date of birth` `the date of the act` `it is proved I knew I ought not to do it`

§§ `378 -- the penalty for stealing`

-- s 378: "Any person who steals anything capable of being stolen is guilty of a crime, and is liable, if no other
-- punishment is provided, to imprisonment for 7 years." Then "Punishment in special cases": (1) a testamentary
-- instrument, 10 years; (2) a motor vehicle driven in a way that is an offence under the Road Traffic Act 1974 s 60, 60A
-- or 61, 8 years; (4a) an aircraft, 10 years; (5) the circumstances (a)-(g), 14 years; (6) a public servant and the
-- Crown's property or property held by virtue of the employment, 10 years; (7) a clerk or servant and the employer's
-- property, 10 years; (8) a director or officer and the company's property, 10 years; (9) property received with a power
-- of attorney or money or proceeds received with a direction, 10 years.
-- Where several special cases apply, the encoding gives the highest (an inference: the Code does not say).
-- Being "in company" with friends is not a s 378 circumstance (it is one in some other sections, not here).
DECLARE `How I stole it` HAS
    `the value in dollars`                                                  IS A NUMBER   -- ss 378(5)(b), 426
    `it is a testamentary instrument`                                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- (1)
    `it is a motor vehicle`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- (2); s 426(3)
    `I drove it in a way that is an offence under the Road Traffic Act 1974 s 60, 60A or 61` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (2): borrowed, asked
    `it is an aircraft`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (4a)
    `I stole it from another person's body`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(a) "from the person of another"
    `I stole it in a dwelling`                                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(b)
    `I used or threatened violence to someone in the dwelling`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(b)
    `I stole it from goods in transit`                                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(c)
    `I stole it from a vessel in distress, wrecked or stranded`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(d)
    `I stole it from a public office where it was kept`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(e)
    `I opened a locked room, box or receptacle with a key or instrument to steal it` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(f)
    `it is a firearm under the Firearms Act 2024 s 6`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- (5)(g): borrowed, asked
    `I am in the Public Service and it is the Crown's or came to me through that job` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (6)
    `I am a clerk or servant and it is my employer's or came to me on my employer's account` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (7)
    `I am a director or officer and it is the company's`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- (8)
    `it came to me with a power of attorney or a direction to apply it`     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (9)
    `my previous stealing convictions in the year before, counting each day once` IS A NUMBER  -- s 426A(2)(b), (4)

GIVEN `h` IS A `How I stole it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 378(5) circumstance applies` IF
       `h`'s `I stole it from another person's body`
    OR (    `h`'s `I stole it in a dwelling`
        AND (   `h`'s `the value in dollars` GREATER THAN `the dwelling value threshold`
             OR `h`'s `I used or threatened violence to someone in the dwelling`))
    OR `h`'s `I stole it from goods in transit`
    OR `h`'s `I stole it from a vessel in distress, wrecked or stranded`
    OR `h`'s `I stole it from a public office where it was kept`
    OR `h`'s `I opened a locked room, box or receptacle with a key or instrument to steal it`
    OR `h`'s `it is a firearm under the Firearms Act 2024 s 6`

GIVEN `h` IS A `How I stole it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ten-year special case applies` IF
       `h`'s `it is a testamentary instrument`
    OR `h`'s `it is an aircraft`
    OR `h`'s `I am in the Public Service and it is the Crown's or came to me through that job`
    OR `h`'s `I am a clerk or servant and it is my employer's or came to me on my employer's account`
    OR `h`'s `I am a director or officer and it is the company's`
    OR `h`'s `it came to me with a power of attorney or a direction to apply it`

GIVEN `h` IS A `How I stole it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I stole a motor vehicle and drove it recklessly or dangerously` IF
        `h`'s `it is a motor vehicle`
    AND `h`'s `I drove it in a way that is an offence under the Road Traffic Act 1974 s 60, 60A or 61`

@export What is the longest imprisonment I can be liable to for stealing, in years (The Criminal Code s 378)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I stole it` @desc What you stole and the circumstances
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most imprisonment for my stealing in years` IS
    IF `a s 378(5) circumstance applies` `how`
    THEN `aggravated stealing years`
    ELSE IF `a ten-year special case applies` `how`
         THEN `special case years`
         ELSE IF `I stole a motor vehicle and drove it recklessly or dangerously` `how`
              THEN `reckless motor vehicle stealing years`
              ELSE `plain stealing years`

§§ `426, 426A, 5 -- summary conviction penalty for stealing`

-- s 426(1): subsection (2) applies to "(a) an offence under section 378 ... in respect of which the greatest term of
-- imprisonment ... does not exceed 7 years; (b) an offence under section 378 to which Item (5)(a), (6), or (7) of that
-- section applies".
-- s 426(2): "where the value of the property in question does not exceed $50 000, unless subsection (4) applies --
-- imprisonment for 2 years and a fine of $24 000."
-- s 426(3): "under section 378 ... where the property in question is a motor vehicle, unless subsection (4) applies --
-- imprisonment for 2 years and a fine of $24 000."
-- s 426(4): "under section 378 ... where the value of the property in question does not exceed $1 000 -- a fine of
-- $6 000." s 426(5): "Subsection (4) is subject to section 426A."
-- s 426A(2), (3): s 426(4) does not apply if the person "has committed, and been convicted of, at least 2 offences that are
-- also stealing offences ... within the period of 1 year before the person's conviction for the current stealing offence";
-- (4)(a) convictions for offences "committed on the same day are to be treated as a single conviction". s 426A(1):
-- "conviction" includes a finding of guilt without a conviction recorded under the Young Offenders Act 1994 s 55.
-- Subsections (3) and (4) are not limited to the offences in subsection (1); read literally, a theft worth $1 000 or less
-- has the fine-only penalty even with a s 378(5) circumstance. That is the reading encoded (an inference from the words).
GIVEN `h` IS A `How I stole it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 426(1) reaches my stealing` IF
       `What is the most imprisonment for my stealing in years` `h` AT MOST `plain stealing years`
    OR `h`'s `I stole it from another person's body`
    OR `h`'s `I am in the Public Service and it is the Crown's or came to me through that job`
    OR `h`'s `I am a clerk or servant and it is my employer's or came to me on my employer's account`

GIVEN `h` IS A `How I stole it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine-only penalty applies` IF
        `h`'s `the value in dollars` AT MOST `the fine-only value ceiling`
    AND `h`'s `my previous stealing convictions in the year before, counting each day once`
            LESS THAN `the previous stealing convictions that end the fine-only penalty`

@export What summary conviction penalty applies to my stealing (The Criminal Code ss 426, 426A)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I stole it` @desc What you stole, its value, the circumstances, and your recent stealing convictions
GIVETH A `Summary penalty`
DECIDE `What summary conviction penalty applies to my stealing` IS
    IF `the fine-only penalty applies` `how`
    THEN `a fine only` 6000
    ELSE IF `how`'s `it is a motor vehicle`
         THEN `imprisonment and a fine` 24 24000
         ELSE IF `s 426(1) reaches my stealing` `how` AND `how`'s `the value in dollars` AT MOST `the summary value ceiling`
              THEN `imprisonment and a fine` 24 24000
              ELSE `no summary conviction penalty`

@export What is the largest fine I face if my stealing is dealt with summarily, in dollars?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I stole it` @desc What you stole, its value, the circumstances, and your recent stealing convictions
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the largest summary fine for my stealing` IS
    CONSIDER `What summary conviction penalty applies to my stealing` `how`
    WHEN `a fine only` f THEN f
    WHEN `imprisonment and a fine` m f THEN f
    WHEN `no summary conviction penalty` THEN 0

@export Can I be imprisoned if my stealing is dealt with summarily?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I stole it` @desc What you stole, its value, the circumstances, and your recent stealing convictions
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be imprisoned on a summary conviction for my stealing` IF
    CONSIDER `What summary conviction penalty applies to my stealing` `how`
    WHEN `imprisonment and a fine` m f THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 5(2): where a summary conviction penalty applies, "the court is to try the charge summarily unless" the court decides
-- under s 5(3) (on an application before plea) that it is to be tried on indictment. Whether it so decides is the court's
-- judgment: asked as a fact. Without a summary conviction penalty the charge is indictable only (s 3, not encoded).
@export Will my stealing charge be tried summarily by a magistrate (The Criminal Code s 5)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I stole it` @desc What you stole, its value, the circumstances, and your recent stealing convictions
      `the court decided under s 5(3) to send it for trial on indictment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on an application before you pleaded, the court decided the charge should be tried on indictment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my stealing charge be tried summarily` IF
    CONSIDER `What summary conviction penalty applies to my stealing` `how`
    WHEN `no summary conviction penalty` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT `the court decided under s 5(3) to send it for trial on indictment`

§§ `221, 80I -- aggravation`

-- s 221(1), in Part V: "circumstances of aggravation means circumstances in which -- (a) the offender is in a family
-- relationship with the victim ...; (b) a child was present when the offence was committed ...; (c) the conduct of the
-- offender ... constituted a breach of an order ... under the Restraining Orders Act 1997 ...; (d) the victim is of or
-- over the age of 60 years." (1A): (a) and (b) do not count where "the offender was a child" and they are the only
-- circumstances. "Family relationship" and the order are borrowed from the Restraining Orders Act 1997: asked as facts.
-- s 444(1A) borrows the s 221 meaning for criminal damage.
-- s 80I, for ss 338B and 444: "circumstances of racial aggravation means circumstances in which -- (a) immediately
-- before or during or immediately after the commission of the offence, the offender demonstrates hostility towards the
-- victim based ... on the victim being a member of a racial group; or (b) the offence is motivated ... by hostility
-- towards persons as members of a racial group."
DECLARE `The circumstances` HAS
    `the offender is in a family relationship with me`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 221(1)(a)
    `a child was present`                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 221(1)(b)
    `it breached a restraining order`                               IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 221(1)(c)
    `I am 60 or older`                                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 221(1)(d)
    `the offender was a child`                                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 221(1A)
    `the offender showed or was moved by hostility to my racial group` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 80I

@export Was the offence against me committed in circumstances of aggravation (The Criminal Code s 221)?
GIVEN `c` IS A `The circumstances` @desc Who the offender is to you, who was there, any restraining order, your age
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it aggravated` IF
       `c`'s `it breached a restraining order`
    OR `c`'s `I am 60 or older`
    OR (    (`c`'s `the offender is in a family relationship with me` OR `c`'s `a child was present`)
        AND (NOT `c`'s `the offender was a child`))

GIVEN `c` IS A `The circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it racially aggravated` IF `c`'s `the offender showed or was moved by hostility to my racial group`

§§ `338, 338A, 338B -- threats`

-- s 338: "a reference to a threat is a reference to a statement or behaviour that expressly constitutes, or may reasonably
-- be regarded as constituting, a threat to -- (a) kill, injure, endanger or harm any person ...; (b) destroy, damage,
-- endanger or harm any property ...; (c) take or exercise control of a building, structure or conveyance by force or
-- violence; (d) cause a detriment of any kind to any person ...; (e) distribute an intimate image ...". Behaviour counts.
-- What the statement or behaviour "may reasonably be regarded" as threatening is for the court: asked as a fact.
DECLARE `What it threatened` IS ONE OF
    `to kill a person`
    `to injure, endanger or harm a person`
    `to destroy, damage, endanger or harm property`
    `to take control of a building, structure or conveyance by force`
    `to cause a person a detriment of any kind`
    `to distribute an intimate image of a person`
    `nothing that s 338 lists`

-- s 338A: "Any person who makes a threat with intent to -- (a) gain a benefit, pecuniary or otherwise, for any person; or
-- (b) cause a detriment ... to any person; or (c) prevent or hinder the doing of an act by a person who is lawfully
-- entitled to do that act; or (d) compel the doing of an act by a person who is lawfully entitled to abstain from doing
-- that act, is guilty of a crime".
-- s 338B(1): "Any person who makes a threat to unlawfully do anything mentioned in section 338(a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) is
-- guilty of a crime".
DECLARE `The threat made to me` HAS
    `what it threatened, expressly or as it may reasonably be regarded` IS A `What it threatened`  -- s 338: a judgment
    `the threatened thing would be unlawful`                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 338B(1) "to unlawfully do"
    `it was meant to gain a benefit for someone`                     IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 338A(a)
    `it was meant to cause someone a detriment`                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 338A(b)
    `it was meant to stop me doing something I am entitled to do`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 338A(c)
    `it was meant to make me do something I am entitled not to do`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 338A(d)
    `the circumstances`                                              IS A `The circumstances`

GIVEN `t` IS A `The threat made to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a threat` IF
    CONSIDER `t`'s `what it threatened, expressly or as it may reasonably be regarded`
    WHEN `nothing that s 338 lists` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `t` IS A `The threat made to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it threatened death` IF
    CONSIDER `t`'s `what it threatened, expressly or as it may reasonably be regarded`
    WHEN `to kill a person` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `t` IS A `The threat made to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it had a s 338A intent` IF
       `t`'s `it was meant to gain a benefit for someone`
    OR `t`'s `it was meant to cause someone a detriment`
    OR `t`'s `it was meant to stop me doing something I am entitled to do`
    OR `t`'s `it was meant to make me do something I am entitled not to do`

DECLARE `Threat offence` IS ONE OF
    `threat with intent to gain etc, s 338A`
    `threats, s 338B`
    `no threat offence`

-- Where both apply, s 338A is the heavier and s 338B is its listed alternative ("Alternative offence: s. 338B"); the
-- encoding names s 338A.
@export What threat offence was committed against me (The Criminal Code ss 338, 338A, 338B)?
GIVEN `the threat` IS A `The threat made to me` @desc What was said or done, what it threatened, what it was meant to achieve, and the circumstances
GIVETH A `Threat offence`
DECIDE `What threat offence was committed against me` IS
    IF `it is a threat` `the threat` AND `it had a s 338A intent` `the threat`
    THEN `threat with intent to gain etc, s 338A`
    ELSE IF `it is a threat` `the threat` AND `the threat`'s `the threatened thing would be unlawful`
         THEN `threats, s 338B`
         ELSE `no threat offence`

-- s 338A penalties: threat to kill, 14 years aggravated, otherwise 10; any other threat, 10 years aggravated, otherwise 7.
-- s 338B(1) penalties: threat to kill, 14 years racially aggravated, 10 aggravated, otherwise 7; any other threat, 6 years
-- racially aggravated, 5 aggravated, otherwise 3. s 338A has no racial aggravation (s 80I does not list it).
@export What is the longest imprisonment the person who threatened me is liable to, in years?
GIVEN `the threat` IS A `The threat made to me` @desc What was said or done, what it threatened, what it was meant to achieve, and the circumstances
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most imprisonment for the threat in years` IS
    CONSIDER `What threat offence was committed against me` `the threat`
    WHEN `threat with intent to gain etc, s 338A` THEN
        IF `it threatened death` `the threat`
        THEN IF `Was it aggravated` (`the threat`'s `the circumstances`) THEN 14 ELSE 10
        ELSE IF `Was it aggravated` (`the threat`'s `the circumstances`) THEN 10 ELSE 7
    WHEN `threats, s 338B` THEN
        IF `it threatened death` `the threat`
        THEN IF `Was it racially aggravated` (`the threat`'s `the circumstances`) THEN 14
             ELSE IF `Was it aggravated` (`the threat`'s `the circumstances`) THEN 10 ELSE 7
        ELSE IF `Was it racially aggravated` (`the threat`'s `the circumstances`) THEN 6
             ELSE IF `Was it aggravated` (`the threat`'s `the circumstances`) THEN 5 ELSE 3
    WHEN `no threat offence` THEN 0

-- s 338B summary conviction penalty: "(a) in a case to which paragraph (a) above applies [a threat to kill]: imprisonment
-- for 3 years and a fine of $36 000; or (b) in a case to which paragraph (b) above applies: imprisonment for 18 months and
-- a fine of $18 000." s 338A provides none.
@export What summary conviction penalty applies to the threat made to me?
GIVEN `the threat` IS A `The threat made to me` @desc What was said or done, what it threatened, what it was meant to achieve, and the circumstances
GIVETH A `Summary penalty`
DECIDE `What summary conviction penalty applies to the threat` IS
    CONSIDER `What threat offence was committed against me` `the threat`
    WHEN `threats, s 338B` THEN
        IF `it threatened death` `the threat`
        THEN `imprisonment and a fine` 36 36000
        ELSE `imprisonment and a fine` 18 18000
    OTHERWISE `no summary conviction penalty`

§§ `444, 445 -- criminal damage and damaging property`

-- s 444(1): "Any person who wilfully and unlawfully destroys or damages any property is guilty of a crime and is liable --
-- (a) if the property is destroyed or damaged by fire, to life imprisonment; or (b) if the property is not destroyed or
-- damaged by fire, to imprisonment for 10 years or, if the offence is committed in circumstances of aggravation or in
-- circumstances of racial aggravation, to imprisonment for 14 years." Summary conviction penalty: where (1)(b) applies and
-- "the amount of the injury done does not exceed $50 000, imprisonment for 3 years and a fine of $36 000."
-- s 445: "A person who unlawfully destroys or damages the property of another person without that other person's consent
-- is guilty of an offence and is liable to imprisonment for 2 years and a fine of $24 000." (A simple offence, and the
-- listed alternative to s 444.)
-- Whether paint or glue "damages" property is for the court: asked as a fact.
DECLARE `The damage done to my property` HAS
    `my property was destroyed or damaged`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- ss 444, 445: a judgment
    `it was done wilfully`                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 444 "wilfully"
    `it was done unlawfully`                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- ss 444, 445 "unlawfully"
    `I consented`                                      IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 445
    `it was done by fire`                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 444(1)(a)
    `the amount of the injury in dollars`              IS A NUMBER   -- s 444 summary conviction penalty
    `the circumstances`                                IS A `The circumstances`

DECLARE `Damage offence` IS ONE OF
    `criminal damage, s 444`
    `damaging property, s 445`
    `no damage offence`

@export What property damage offence was committed against me (The Criminal Code ss 444, 445)?
GIVEN `the damage` IS A `The damage done to my property` @desc What was damaged, how, whether wilfully, and the circumstances
GIVETH A `Damage offence`
DECIDE `What damage offence was committed against me` IS
    IF     `the damage`'s `my property was destroyed or damaged`
       AND `the damage`'s `it was done unlawfully`
       AND `the damage`'s `it was done wilfully`
    THEN `criminal damage, s 444`
    ELSE IF     `the damage`'s `my property was destroyed or damaged`
            AND `the damage`'s `it was done unlawfully`
            AND (NOT `the damage`'s `I consented`)
         THEN `damaging property, s 445`
         ELSE `no damage offence`

@export What is the longest imprisonment the person who damaged my property is liable to?
GIVEN `the damage` IS A `The damage done to my property` @desc What was damaged, how, whether wilfully, and the circumstances
GIVETH A `Maximum imprisonment`
DECIDE `What is the most imprisonment for the damage` IS
    CONSIDER `What damage offence was committed against me` `the damage`
    WHEN `criminal damage, s 444` THEN
        IF `the damage`'s `it was done by fire`
        THEN `life imprisonment`
        ELSE IF    `Was it aggravated` (`the damage`'s `the circumstances`)
                OR `Was it racially aggravated` (`the damage`'s `the circumstances`)
             THEN `years of imprisonment` 14
             ELSE `years of imprisonment` 10
    WHEN `damaging property, s 445` THEN `years of imprisonment` 2
    WHEN `no damage offence` THEN `years of imprisonment` 0

@export What summary conviction penalty applies to the damage done to my property?
GIVEN `the damage` IS A `The damage done to my property` @desc What was damaged, how, whether wilfully, the amount of the injury, and the circumstances
GIVETH A `Summary penalty`
DECIDE `What summary conviction penalty applies to the damage` IS
    CONSIDER `What damage offence was committed against me` `the damage`
    WHEN `criminal damage, s 444` THEN
        IF     (NOT `the damage`'s `it was done by fire`)
           AND `the damage`'s `the amount of the injury in dollars` AT MOST `the damage summary ceiling`
        THEN `imprisonment and a fine` 36 36000
        ELSE `no summary conviction penalty`
    -- s 445 is a simple offence, dealt with summarily; its only penalty is the one it states.
    WHEN `damaging property, s 445` THEN `imprisonment and a fine` 24 24000
    WHEN `no damage offence` THEN `no summary conviction penalty`
